            "review_text": "cherry0203\nQuang Ninh Province, Vietnam9 contributions\n0\nGood design, poor maintainance\nMar 2018 • Solo\nThe place is designed by the well-known Vietnamese architect Vo Trong Nghia, the same one created bamboo house in Flamingo Dai Lai. However it looks like being more poorly maintained. The water pond around isn't clean and most tables and chairs is oil stained. \nThe air-flow is a problem too. If you'd like a coffee, better come at later than 10:00am because when they serve breakfast the whole place is full with food smell (including fish sauce smell) so it's not very nice. \nGood place to take picture for Instagram though, bad if you just want good drink in a quite place.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 21, 2018",
